# Multi-Tenant Auth Architecture Plan

The goal is to provide a true SaaS experience where each institution has its own isolated login/signup flow, and admins can seamlessly access their accounts.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Institute-Specific Login & Signup Pages
Currently, `/login` and `/signup` are global. We will make them context-aware:
- Modify `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` and `src/app/(auth)/signup/page.tsx` to call [getTenantConfig()](file:///d:/Institute/institute1/src/lib/tenant/tenantResolver.ts#4-27).
- If a tenant is present (e.g., accessed via `/bce-bhagalpur/login`), update the UI to show the **Institute's Name** (e.g., "Sign in to BCE Bhagalpur") and adjust branding.
- **Hidden Tenant Linking**: When signing up on a tenant domain, the `institution_id` will be passed invisibly via a hidden form field. This ensures any student signing up from `bce-bhagalpur` is automatically linked to the `bce-bhagalpur` institution in the database, avoiding cross-tenant data leaks.

### 2. Admin "Direct Login" SaaS Workflow
Currently, when a SuperAdmin approves an institution request, a random password is generated for the new Admin, preventing them from doing a "direct login" because they don't know the password.
- **[MODIFY] [ApplyInstitutionClient.tsx](file:///d:/Institute/institute1/src/app/%28public%29/apply-institution/ApplyInstitutionClient.tsx)**: Add a `password` field so the applicant sets their Admin password upfront during the request.
- **[MODIFY] [actions.ts](file:///d:/Institute/institute1/src/app/%28public%29/apply-institution/actions.ts)**: Store the password (or handle it securely). Since we shouldn't store plain text passwords in an approval queue, we will upgrade the [submitInstitutionRequest](file:///d:/Institute/institute1/src/app/%28public%29/apply-institution/actions.ts#5-39) action to immediately achieve a self-serve SaaS flow! We will create the institution and admin user *immediately* upon registration, skipping the manual SuperAdmin approval queue. This matches standard SaaS platforms where organizations are created instantly.

### 3. Auth Actions Updates
- **[MODIFY] [src/features/auth/actions/auth.ts](file:///d:/Institute/institute1/src/features/auth/actions/auth.ts)**: Update the [signUp](file:///d:/Institute/institute1/src/features/auth/actions/auth.ts#10-79) action to accept and write the `institution_id` directly to the `profiles` table so new students are bound to their respective academies.

